{"name":"Oregon Hazel","hex":"#916238","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hazel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree or shrub of the genus Corylus, bearing edible nuts called hazelnuts or filberts.","The nut of the hazel tree."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-brown colour. (often used to refer to eye colour)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oregon","blocks":[{"text":"Oregon is a state in the Pacific Northwest region of the United States. It is a part of the Western United States, with the Columbia River delineating much of Oregon's northern boundary with Washington, while the Snake River delineates much of its eastern boundary with Idaho. The 42° north parallel delineates the southern boundary with California and Nevada. The western boundary is formed by the Pacific Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Flag_of_Oregon.svg/330px-Flag_of_Oregon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oregon","wikidata":"Q824"},{"title":"Hazel","blocks":[{"text":"Hazels are plants of the genus Corylus of deciduous trees and large shrubs native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere. The genus is usually placed in the birch family, Betulaceae, though some botanists split the hazels into a separate family Corylaceae. The fruit of the hazel is the hazelnut; the trees are also grown as ornaments in hedges or gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Corylus_avellana_0001.JPG/330px-Corylus_avellana_0001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazel","wikidata":"Q145889"},{"title":"Eye color","blocks":[{"text":"Eye color is a polygenic phenotypic trait determined by two factors: the pigmentation of the eye's iris and the frequency-dependence of the scattering of light by the turbid medium in the stroma of the iris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg/330px-Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_color","wikidata":"Q23786"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/2005_OR_Proof.png/500px-2005_OR_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/2005_OR_Proof.png/500px-2005_OR_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2005_OR_Proof.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/2014-07-06_14_49_35_View_north_along_Harney_County_Route_201_%28Fields-Denio_Road%29_at_the_end_of_Nevada_State_Route_292_%28Denio_Road%29_at_the_Oregon_border_in_Denio%2C_Nevada.JPG/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/2014-07-06_14_49_35_View_north_along_Harney_County_Route_201_%28Fields-Denio_Road%29_at_the_end_of_Nevada_State_Route_292_%28Denio_Road%29_at_the_Oregon_border_in_Denio%2C_Nevada.JPG/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/2014-07-06_14_49_35_View_north_along_Harney_County_Route_201_%28Fields-Denio_Road%29_at_the_end_of_Nevada_State_Route_292_%28Denio_Road%29_at_the_Oregon_border_in_Denio%2C_Nevada.JPG/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Oregon border welcome sign at Denio, Nevada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2014-07-06_14_49_35_View_north_along_Harney_County_Route_201_(Fields-Denio_Road)_at_the_end_of_Nevada_State_Route_292_(Denio_